Add a regression guard for tile seams in a stack

The mosaic that shipped was invisible to every metric already in the suite:
the image stayed sharp and correlated with a single frame. It was only
*locally* wrong, at the tile boundaries. So the guard measures exactly that:
the mean horizontal gradient **on tile boundaries** divided by the mean
gradient **inside tiles**.

A continuous image scores near 1; a stack whose tiles disagree scores clearly
higher. On the synthetic case the metric separates clean (1.60) from seamed
(3.74), a 2.3x gap, and the test asserts that separation rather than a brittle
absolute threshold on a synthetic baseline.

Honest note: my first attempt at this guard was useless. I wrote a
correlation-against-a-reference-frame test, and both the correct and the broken
stack scored 0.999, because a smooth disc survives a few pixels of drift. It
would never have caught the bug. The replacement targets the actual failure
signature.

22 tests pass.
